desc: Round Trip Circular Auto-Panner (mda RoundPan port) by chmaha
tags: pan auto-pan rotation stereo modulation
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  A circular panner. The input is summed to mono and placed on a circle around the listener: 0° is centre front,
  -90° and +90° are hard left and right, and towards ±180° the two channels move into anti-phase, which sounds
  diffuse and "behind". Pan sets the position; Auto rotates the sound around the circle, clockwise to the right of
  centre and anticlockwise to the left, at up to about 515 degrees per second. The middle of the Auto range
  (45 to 55 %) stops the rotation. Moving Pan restarts the rotation from the new position.
  Ported from mda RoundPan by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects
  https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
